From 9490976cfaf654e8bed740b0259619c0b6932319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: syn <syn@syn.as>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:35:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=94=A5=20refactor(generate)!:=20remov?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20the=20plain-text=20fallback=20rung?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The attempt ladder ended in a plain-text rung 'for models that reject
structured output': an 'Output ONLY the command itself ... no markdown,
no code fences, no quotes, no preamble, no explanation' prompt variant,
an ===OPTION=== delimiter protocol, cleanCommand's fence/quote regex
cleanup, and a parallel safety path for the unassessed candidates it
produced (modelAssessed, modelSignalAvailable, decideAction's
refuse-unassessed, and three degraded-signal notes).

That is the JSON-forcing stack structured outputs replace, and its
stated trigger no longer exists: the Agent SDK delivers outputFormat
through an end-turn tool call, which every tool-capable Claude model
supports (verified live on claude-sonnet-5). The rung therefore only
ever caught failures of the structured call - auth, overload,
error_max_turns, or a structured reply whose commands normaliseCommand
had rejected - and answered them with a command carrying no model
danger verdict. Worse, cleanCommand kept the first non-empty line of a
multi-line reply, so a structured command rejected precisely because it
spanned lines could come back truncated: the opposite of
normaliseCommand's reject-don't-truncate rule.

The model-facing prompts are byte-for-byte unchanged on the structured
path (checked mechanically). A failed or unusable response is now an
AicmdError, one call and no hidden retry.

- generate: one structured call; no ladder, no cost summing
- prompts: drop OPTION_DELIMITER, the structured flag, the plain
  prompt variants, cleanCommand and plainToCandidates
- types/safety/cli/interactive: drop modelAssessed,
  modelSignalAvailable, refuse-unassessed and the degraded notes
- index: stop re-exporting the removed helpers
- tests: replace fallback cases with 'errors surface, exactly one call'
- AGENTS.md invariant, README, design spec (pipeline, safety model,
  testing, decisions log)

BREAKING CHANGE: cleanCommand, plainToCandidates, OPTION_DELIMITER,
buildUser's third parameter, SystemPromptOptions.structured,
GeneratedCommand.modelAssessed, DangerAssessment.modelSignalAvailable
and the 'refuse-unassessed' PlainAction are gone from the library
surface; a generation failure is an error instead of a degraded command.
